$DATUM Flow Mode. β -Aminoethanol 1 (5 2.0 g , 851 mmol , 5 1.4 mL) and
acetonylacetone 2 (9 7.3 g , 852 mmol, 1 00 m L) were pumped into the
MJOD reactor utilizing standard piston pumps at a rate of 0.71 and 1.38
mL min -1 , respectively. The reaction was conducted at room temperature
with a residence time of 18 min, that corresponds to a overall flow rate
of 2.1 mL min -1 . The collected reaction mixture was distilled under
reduced pressure (p =1 mm Hg), first at a temperatureof 40 °C in order to
remove water produced under the reaction, then the product 3 was col
lected at 84 °C, to achieve a quantitative yield (2837 mmol h -1) of
target product .
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM batch mode gave lower yield (74%), flow system used, Paal-Knorr
condensation, multijet oscillating disk reactor used
