$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1.2 General method of Paal-Knorr reaction 2,5-Hexanedione 3.0 mmol, amine
3.0 mmol and formic acid 0.45 mmol were added to a 50 mL round-bottom
flask successively, then stirred for 0.5-6 h at room temperature, and
traced by TLC. After reaction, the mixture was washed with cold saturated
NaHCO3 solution (15 mL × 2) and ice water (15 mL × 3) successively, then
placed in a vacuum dryer with anhydrous calcium chloride at room
temperature to give the pure compound 3a-3k. 3a, 83 % m.p. 41-42 °C
(lit.[6b]: 42-44 °C); 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz) δ: 7.33-7.23 (m, 3H),
6.91-6.89 (m, 2H), 5.87 (s, 2H), 5.03 (s, 2H), 2.17 (s, 6H); ESI-MS m/z:
186 [M + H]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry, green chemistry-catalyst, Paal-Knorr reaction, no
solvent, optimization study, optimized on time
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A highly efficient Paal-Knorr synthesis of pyrroles catalyzed by formic
acid at room temperature under solvent-free conditions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
