$DATUM 64-18-6
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 1.2 General method of Paal-Knorr reaction
2,5-Hexanedione 3.0 mmol, amine 3.0 mmol and formic acid 0.45 mmol were
added to a 50 mL round-bottom flask successively, then stirred for 0.5-6
h at room temperature, and traced by TLC. After reaction, the mixture was
washed with cold saturated NaHCO3 solution (15 mL × 2) and ice water (15
mL × 3) successively, then placed in a vacuum dryer with anhydrous
calcium chloride at room temperature to give the pure compound 3a-3k. 3c,
91 % m.p. 46-47 °C (lit.[11a]: 46 °C); 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz) δ: 7.27
(d, J = 7.8 Hz, 2H), 7.11 (d, J = 8.1 Hz, 2H), 5.91 (s, 2H), 2.45 (s,
3H), 2.06 (s, 6H); ESI-MS m/z: 186 [M + H]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry, green chemistry-catalyst, Paal-Knorr reaction, no
solvent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A highly efficient Paal-Knorr synthesis of pyrroles catalyzed by formic
acid at room temperature under solvent-free conditions
