$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Methyl 5-tert-butyl-2-(2-phenyethyl)furane-3-carboxylate. 12 Product 5
(0.5 g, 1,64 mmol) was dissolved into EtOH (2 mL) into a 50 mL
roundbottom flask equipped with a stir bar and a reflux condenser. HCl
0.1 mL of a 37% solution) was added and the flask inserted into the
cavity of a Discovery Microwave System apparatus (from CEM) and heated at
150 W for 4 min (internal temperature 100°C). The mixture was diluted
with AcOEt and the solvent washed several times with a saturated solution
of NaHCO3. The organic layer was dried over anhydrous Na2SO4 and the
solvent evaporated. The 1H NMR spectrum of the crude showed the presence
of pure furan 10 that could be eventually additionally purified by flash
chromatography (eluent Hexane: AcOEt 8: 1, Rf = 0.75). Obtained 0.49 g,
95% yield. 1H NMR spectrum enclosed. Methyl
5-tert-butyl-2-(2-phenyethyl)furane-3-carboxylate. 12, yield yield 0.49
g, 95%. eluent Hexane: AcOEt 8: 1, Rf = 0.75.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Microwave-assisted Paal-Knorr reaction. A rapid approach to substituted
pyrroles and furans
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Minetto, Giacomo; Raveglia, Luca F.; Taddei, Maurizio
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2004), 6(3), 389-392

