$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of Model Compound. Pyrrolic furan was first obtained by the
reaction of 2,5-hexanedione (5 g, 44 mmol) and furfurylamine (4.26 g, 44
mmol) without using any solvent in a 50 mL round-bottomed flask equipped
with a magnetic stirrer. The reaction mixture was heated to 70 °C for 20
h with vigorous stirring. After the reaction, the mixture was diluted
with dichloromethane (150 mL) and dried over sodium sulfate. The solvent
was removed under vacuum to yield pyrrolic furan. Yield 7.06 g, 94%. 1H
NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3, δ): 7.33 (dd, 1H, J = 1.8 Hz, J = 1.1 Hz), 6.29 (dd,
1H, J = 3.2 Hz, J = 1.8 Hz), 6.03 (m, 1H), 5.81(s, 2H), 4.91 (d, 2H, J =
0.7 Hz), 2.27 (s, 6H). 13C NMR (100.6 Hz, CDCl3, δ): 151.3, 142.1, 127.8,
110.2, 106.9, 105.3, 40.4, 12.3. Elemental analysis for C11H13NO: Calcd:
C, 75.40; H, 7.48; N, 7.99; Found: C, 75.12; H, 7.38; N, 7.89.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Paal-Knorr reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Thermally Self-Healing Polymeric Materials: The Next Step to Recycling
Thermoset Polymers?
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Zhang, Youchun; Broekhuis, Antonius A.; Picchioni, Francesco
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Macromolecules (Washington, DC, United States) (2009), 42(6), 1906-1912

