$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-methyl-3,5-diphenylfuran. Compound 10: Following a procedure from
Taddei and coworkersS15 1,3-diphenylpentane-1,4-dione (78 mg, 0.31 mmol)
was dissolved in 1.33 mL of 200-proof ethanol and transferred to a
microwave vial charged with a stir bar. 0.33 mL of 1M HCl was added, and
after vial was sealed, the mixture was heated in a microwave at 150 °C
for 15 minutes. The crude reaction mixture was then diluted with EtOAc,
and washed with aqueous saturated sodium bicarbonate and then brine. The
organic layer was then dried over Na2SO4 and the solvent was then removed
in vacuo, yielding the product without further purification (61 mg, 0.26
mmol, 85% yield). Spectral data matched that previously reported.S2
2-methyl-3,5-diphenylfuran, yield 61 mg, 0.26 mmol, 85%
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, Paal-Knorr cyclization, literature preparation,
sealed tube used
