$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the preparation of
1H-pyrroles 5a-f: A mixture of the α,δ-ketoester 2 (0.4 mmol), the
corresponding amine or ammonium acetate (2 mmol) and acetic acid (0.1 ml)
in a closed vessel was irradiated in a monomode microwave oven at 150 W
for 12 min. and at 90 °C. After finishing the irradiation, the mixture
was allowed to reach room temperature and the vessel was opened. Ethyl
acetate (20 ml) was added and the resulting solution was washed with
NaHCO3 (3 x 20 ml, saturated aqueous solution), dried over Na2SO4 and
evaporated under reduced pressure, to obtain the corresponding product 5.
Ethyl 3-(4-hydroxyphenyl)-5-phenyl-1H-pyrrole-2-carboxylate (5f). Yield:
81 %. Violet solid; m. p. 205-206°C; νmax/cm-1 (KBr) 3361, 2997, 2980,
1662, 1276, 1228.1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3+DMSO-d6) δ = 10.39 (s, 1H), 8.77
(s, 1H), 7.70 (d, J = 7.5, 2H), 7.41 (dd, J = 16.7, 8.1, 4H), 7.28 (t, J
= 7.3, 1H), 6.84 (d, J = 8.4, 2H), 6.55 (d, J = 2.7, 1H), 4.26 (q, J =
7.1, 2H), 1.28 (t, J = 7.1, 3H).13C NMR (126 MHz, CDCl3+DMSO-d6) δ =
160.9, 156.2, 135.2, 133.1, 131.0, 130.2, 130.1, 128.4, 127.2, 126.0,
124.8, 118.0, 114.5, 114.4, 109.2, 59.6, 14.0. Anal. Calcd. For
C19H17NO3: C, 74.3; H, 5.6; N, 4.6. Found: C, 74.5 ; H, 5.5; N, 4.6.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation (150W), Paal-Knorr reaction;, sealed tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Formation of γ-Oxoacids and 1H-Pyrrol-2(5H)-ones from α,β-Unsaturated
Ketones and Ethyl Nitroacetate
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
