$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of thiophenes: To the diketone 3
(400 mg, 0.44 mequiv/g) in toluene (4 mL), was added Lawesson's reagent
(356 mg, 0.88 mmol) and the mixture was heated at reflux for 24 h. The
resin was collected by filtration and washed as mentioned above to afford
the thiophene 3T on solid support (400 mg). Cleavage and workup afforded
the crude product which was purified by column chromatography using 5%
EtOAc-petroleum ether as the eluent to afford thiophene 3T. The resin
bound furan (395 mg) was suspended in 25% TFA/ CH2Cl2 and stirred at r.t.
for 4 h. The resin was filtered and washed with CH2Cl2 (3 × 10 mL). The
combined filtrates were washed successively with sat. aq NaHCO3, water,
brine, and dried over Na2SO4. Evaporation under reduced pressure afforded
the crude product, which was purified by column chromatography using 3%
EtOAc-petroleum ether as eluent to afford furan 1F. Yield, 110 mg, 80%.
1H NMR (200 MHz, CDCl3) δ 0.92 (t, J = 6.8 Hz, 3 H), 1.35-1.52 (m, 2 H),
1.62-1.80 (m, 2 H), 2.88 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 2 H), 6.80 (d, J = 8.5 Hz, 2 H),
7.08 (s, 1 H), 7.28-7.50 (m, 7 H). 13C NMR (50 MHz, CDCl3) δ 13.8, 22.4,
28.2, 34.3, 115.6, 124.1, 126.7, 126.9, 128.3, 128.7, 137.1, 139.3,
139.6, 139.9, 154.9. m/z (EI) 308 (78), 265 (100).
