$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of furans: To the 1,4-diketone 1, on the solid-support3 (400
mg, 0.44 mequiv/g) suspended in toluene (4 mL), p-TSA (105 mg, 0.53 mmol)
was added and the mixture was heated at reflux for 24 h. The resin was
then filtered and washed successively with CH2Cl2 (2 × 10 mL), 1:1
CH2Cl2-MeOH (2 × 10 mL), MeOH (2 × 10 mL), CH2Cl2 (2 × 10 mL) and finally
with diethyl ether (2 × 10 mL). The resin bound furan (395 mg) was
suspended in 25% TFA/ CH2Cl2 and stirred at r.t. for 4 h. The resin was
filtered and washed with CH2Cl2 (3 × 10 mL). The combined filtrates were
washed successively with sat. aq NaHCO3, water, brine, and dried over
Na2SO4. Evaporation under reduced pressure afforded the crude product,
which was purified by column chromatography using 3% EtOAc-petroleum
ether as eluent to afford furan 1F. Yield, 100 mg, 74%. 1H NMR (200 MHz,
CDCl3) d 0.90 (t, J = 7.0 Hz, 3 H), 1.25-1.48 (m, 6 H), 1.72-1.90 (m, 2
H), 2.85 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 2 H), 6.72 (m, 1 H), 7.12-7.45 (m, 9 H).13C NMR
(50 MHz, CDCl3) d 14.0, 22.5, 27.0, 28.5, 29.0, 31.5, 107.0, 110.3,
114.0, 116.0, 123.0, 126.5, 127.7, 128.5, 130.0, 132.5, 134.1, 151.1,
152.0, 155.9. m/z (EI) 320 (5), 248 (10), 84 (61).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM combinatorial, solid-supported reactant, optimization study, optimized on
reagent, stoichiometry
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Solid-phase synthesis of heterocycles from 1,4-diketone synthons
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Raghavan, Sadagopan; Anuradha, K.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synlett (2003), (5), 711-713

