$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Preparation of 1H-Pyrrol-2(5H)-ones 4a-h. A
mixture of the γ-ketoacid 3 (0.4 mmol), the corresponding amine or
ammonium acetate (2 mmol), and acetic acid (0.1 mL) in a closed vessel
was irradiated in a monomode microwave oven at 150 W for the time and at
the temperature reported in Table 1. After finishing the irradiation, the
mixture was allowed to reach room temperature and the vessel was opened.
Ethyl acetate (20 mL) was added and the resulting solution was washed
with NaHCO3 (3 x 20 mL, saturated aqueous solution), dried over Na2SO4,
and evaporated under reduced pressure to obtain the corresponding product
4. 3-(4-Methoxyphenyl)-5-phenyl-1,5-dihydro-2H-pyrrol-2-one (4a): yield
72%, white solid. mp 188-190 °C; νmax/cm-1 (KBr) 3193, 3054, 2932, 1678,
1261, 1035; 1H NMR (500MHz, MeOD) δ 7.84 (d, J = 8.4Hz, 2H), 7.44-7.22
(m, 6H), 6.94 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H), 5.32 (s, 1H), 3.82 (s, 3H); 13C NMR
(126 MHz, MeOD) δ 179.3, 169.1, 149.9, 147.0, 145.0, 142.2, 138.6, 138.1,
138.0, 137.8, 137.2, 137.0, 136.8, 133.5, 123.4, 64.7, 53.0. Anal.Calcd
for C17H15NO2:C, 77.0; H, 5.7; N, 5.3 . Found: C, 76.8; H, 5.4; N,5.6.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation (150W), Paal-Knorr reaction;, sealed tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Formation of γ-Oxoacids and 1H-Pyrrol-2(5H)-ones from α,β-Unsaturated
Ketones and Ethyl Nitroacetate
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Aginagalde, Maialen; Bello, Tamara; Masdeu, Carme; Vara, Yosu; Arrieta,
Ana; Cossio, Fernando P.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2010), 75(21), 7435-7438

