$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of furans: To the 1,4-diketone 1, on
the solid-support3 (400 mg, 0.44 mequiv/g) suspended in toluene (4 mL),
p-TSA (105 mg, 0.53 mmol) was added and the mixture was heated at reflux
for 24 h. The resin was then filtered and washed successively with CH2Cl2
(2 × 10 mL), 1:1 CH2Cl2-MeOH (2 × 10 mL), MeOH (2 × 10 mL), CH2Cl2 (2 ×
10 mL) and finally with diethyl ether (2 × 10 mL). The resin bound furan
(395 mg) was suspended in 25% TFA/ CH2Cl2 and stirred at r.t. for 4 h.
The resin was filtered and washed with CH2Cl2 (3 × 10 mL). The combined
filtrates were washed successively with sat. aq NaHCO3, water, brine, and
dried over Na2SO4. Evaporation under reduced pressure afforded the crude
product, which was purified by column chromatography using 3%
EtOAc-petroleum ether as eluent to afford furan 1F. 3F, yield 71%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM combinatorial, solid-supported reactant, optimization study, optimized on
reagent, stoichiometry
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Solid-phase synthesis of heterocycles from 1,4-diketone synthons
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Raghavan, Sadagopan; Anuradha, K.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synlett (2003), (5), 711-713

