$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of pyrroles: To the suspension of
the diketone 2 (400 mg, 0.46 mequiv/g) suspended in dry toluene (4 mL)
was added n-butyl amine (500 mg, 6.9 mmol) followed by p-TSA (110 mg,
0.55 mmol). The mixture was heated at reflux for 24 h, the resin
collected by filtration and washed as detailed earlier to afford the
pyrrole 2PB on solid-support (420 mg). Cleavage and workup afforded the
crude product which was purified by column chromatography using 3%
EtOAc-petroleum ether as the eluent to afford pyrrole 2PB. The resin
bound furan (395 mg) was suspended in 25% TFA/ CH2Cl2 and stirred at r.t.
for 4 h. The resin was filtered and washed with CH2Cl2 (3 × 10 mL). The
combined filtrates were washed successively with sat. aq NaHCO3, water,
brine, and dried over Na2SO4. Evaporation under reduced pressure afforded
the crude product, which was purified by column chromatography using 3%
EtOAc-petroleum ether as eluent to afford furan 1F. 2PB,yield 70%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM combinatorial, Paal-Knorr reaction first stage, solid-supported reactant
